  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the divergence found:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`): dispatches on `options.version`/`legacy` \u2014 `legacy: true` (or `version: \"legacy\"`) routes to `transformer-legacy.ts` (stage-2 form, `@babel/plugin-syntax-decorators` inherited); anything else (`2018-09`/`2021-12`/\u2026/`2023-11`) goes through `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3/TC39 form). Critically, `transformer-legacy.ts` contains **no `Reflect.metadata`/`design:paramtypes` emission logic at all** \u2014 Babel's decorator transform (legacy or not) never emits TypeScript's `emitDecoratorMetadata` output natively. `@babel/preset-typescript` (`babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts`) only wires in `@babel/plugin-transform-typescript`, which strips types; it has no decorator-metadata pass either. So for NestJS DI to work under Babel, metadata emission must come from a separate plugin (e.g. `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`) placed before the decorators plugin \u2014 plain \"Babel + preset-typescript + plugin-proposal-decorators(legacy:true)\" silently produces classes with decorators applied but **zero** `design:*` metadata, i.e. the same failure mode as the customer's SWC report.\n\n**SWC side**: `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` wires `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` \u2192 `decorators::Config.legacy` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` \u2192 `decorators::Config.emit_metadata`, both **defaulting to `false`**. In `swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs::decorators()`: if `c.legacy` is false, the new-proposal `Decorators` fold runs and `emit_metadata: true` is `unimplemented!()` (i.e., metadata is only ever possible under the legacy path). Only when `legacy: true` does it dispatch into `legacy::new(emit_metadata)` (`legacy/mod.rs`), whose `TscDecorator::visit_mut_class` conditionally runs `Metadata::new(...)` (`legacy/metadata.rs`) to synthesize the `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` decorators (emitted via the `ts_metadata` helper) \u2014 mirroring TypeScript's own `emitDecoratorMetadata` behavior, ported from `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`.\n\n**Root cause**: NestJS requires *both* `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true` in `.swcrc`'s `jsc.transform`. If the customer's SWC config only set `legacyDecorator: true` (to match `experimentalDecorators` in tsconfig) but left `decoratorMetadata` at its default `false` \u2014 or omitted `legacyDecorator` entirely, leaving SWC on the stage-3 path where metadata emission is structurally impossible \u2014 decorators fire (classes still construct) but no `Reflect.metadata`/`design:paramtypes` payload is ever attached, so Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata('design:paramtypes', \u2026)` returns `undefined` and DI resolution crashes exactly as reported.",
